message.content:
- Failures recur when the agent holds the target but keeps searching, examining, or placing it in wrong receptacles instead of using the available transform or final put.
- Maintain reusable stages: find_target, take_target, transform, go_destination, put_target, wrong_inventory, plus transformed and pick_two placed counts/locations.
- on_init gives task order guidance; on_post_step updates stage from actions/inventory/world facts; make_pre_hint gives deduped subgoal nudges; on_before_action blocks only invalid/unlisted or premature/wrong-destination target actions.
- Avoid regression by not forcing numbered ALFWorld actions and by soft-guiding only when inventory, admissible actions, and stage evidence make the next subgoal clear.
